            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Surgical approach;ventral method is articulation: (1) dorsal: displacement of the preferred. spinous process of the axis; (2) ventral:",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Ventral approach—variety of methods: increased size of the occipito-atlas-axis joint cavity.",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Allows identification of spinal cord",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "compression.",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Allows recognition of secondary spinal",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "cord pathology such as edema, hemorrhage, or gliosis, which may impact prognosis.",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "CT—may provide detailed visualization of bony structures, which allows for creation of three-dimensional reconstructed image to help surgical planning.",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Dorsal approach—use wire or synthetic",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
