          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "PRECAUTIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "PRECAUTIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "suture material to fix spinous process of axis",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Proper positioning will require sedation",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "to dorsal arch of atlas; provides less rigid or general anesthesia. fixation and may be associated with greater",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Sedation or general anesthesia carries",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "implant failure. significant risk for iatrogenic trauma.",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Strict exercise restriction required for",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Care needs to be exercised when",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "first month postoperatively, followed by positioning animals. gradual return to activity over additional",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Avoid excessive flexion of the neck!",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "month.",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Flexion may exacerbate compression,",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Adjunctive medication (see below). which may worsen clinical signs or cause",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Overall prognosis ranges from 63% to 91% death due to spinal cord trauma. success—improved prognosis associated with",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "To protect against neck flexion during",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "young (<24 months) dogs, duration of clinical",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "recovery, affected animals should be closely",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "young (<24 months) dogs, duration of clinical"
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "signs<10 months, and mild neurologic",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "monitored until they are capable of",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "signs<10 months, and mild neurologic"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "deficits.",
              "pdf_page": 214,
              "printed_page": 132,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "signs<10 months, and mild neurologic"
